module

public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.Triangulated
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.YonedaHomCohomology
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.DifferentialGraded.RightModule.YonedaImageQuotient
public import StacksFrontier.CategoryTheory.Triangulated.LocalReflectorHom

/-!
# The chain `(*)` of [Stacks, Tag 09LK], composed

Let `C` be a differential graded category over a commutative ring `R` whose objects and whose
morphism modules live in one universe, let `G` be a family of objects of `C` indexed by that
universe, and let `N = ⟨h_{G i}⟩` be the localizing subcategory of `K(Mod^dg(C))` generated by
the attached representables. Write `Z = Φ⁻¹ N` for the objects of `K(C)` whose representable
lies in `N`, and let `q : K(C) ⥤ DA` be a localization of `K(C)` at the morphisms whose cone
lies in `Z`, commuting with the shift.

Step 1 of the replacement proof of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] displays the identification

`(*)  H^n((L h_y)(x)) = Hom_{K(Mod^dg(C))}(h_x, (L h_y)⟦n⟧) = Hom_{K(Mod^dg(C))/N}(Q h_x, Q h_y⟦n⟧)
       = Hom_{DA}(q x, (q y)⟦n⟧)`

for `L` a reflector onto the `N`-local objects. This file composes the three links into one
bijection. Nothing is added to the hypotheses of the three: in particular no resolution
hypothesis on `K(C)` is used, and the reflector and its unit have disappeared from the
right-hand side.

## The three links

* the differential graded Yoneda lemma,
  `DGCategory.RightModule.homShiftEquivEvaluationGradedCohomology`, which identifies the
  explicit degree-`n` cohomology of the complex `(L h_y)(x)` — written as the evaluation
  `ev_x (L h_y)` — with `Hom_{K(Mod^dg(C))}(h_x, (L h_y)⟦n⟧)`;
* the reflector comparison, `CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty.homEquivReflectorShift`, which
  removes `L` in favour of the Verdier quotient at `N`;
* the source-side comparison, `DGCategory.RightModule.homEquivDerivedYonedaOnK'`, which
  identifies the Hom groups of that quotient between representables with the Hom groups of any
  localization of `K(C)` at `Z`.

## Main definitions

* `DGCategory.RightModule.chainEquivReflectorEvaluation`: **the composite `(*)`.**

## Main results

* `DGCategory.RightModule.exists_chainEquivReflectorEvaluation`: the composite together with the
  reflector that step 1 produces, so that the only remaining datum is the localization `q`.

## Universes

`C : DGCategory.{v, v} R` with `G` indexed by `Type v`, which is the condition step 1 carries
through Brown representability
(`DGCategory.RightModule.exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK_of_dgCategory`). The
localization `q` may land in any universe.

## What this does *not* supply

The right-hand side is a Hom group of a localization of `K(C)` at `Z = Φ⁻¹ N`. Reading it as a
Hom group of the derived category of an abelian category needs `Z` to be the acyclic complexes,
which is `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_eq` in
`StacksFrontier/CategoryTheory/DifferentialGraded/RightModule/YonedaKernelAcyclic.lean` and is
proved there only under the existence of `Ac`-resolutions. That hypothesis is not used here and
is not discharged here.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Tag 09LK](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/09LK)
-/

@[expose] public noncomputable section

namespace DGCategory

universe v' u' v r

open CategoryTheory CategoryTheory.Limits CategoryTheory.Pretriangulated
open CategoryTheory.ObjectProperty

variable {R : Type r} [CommRing R]

namespace RightModule

section

variable (C : DGCategory.{v, v} R) [Preadditive C.K] [HasZeroObject C.K] [HasShift C.K ℤ]
  [∀ n : ℤ, (shiftFunctor C.K n).Additive] [Pretriangulated C.K]
  [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).CommShift ℤ] [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).IsTriangulated]
  {ι : Type v} (G : ι → C.Obj)

/-- **The chain `(*)` of [Stacks, Tag 09LK], composed.** Let `N` be the localizing subcategory
of `K(Mod^dg(C))` generated by the representables `h_{G i}`, let `L` be a reflector onto the
`N`-local objects with unit `η` whose fibres lie in `N`, and let `q : K(C) ⥤ DA` be a
localization of `K(C)` at the morphisms whose cone lies in `Z = Φ⁻¹ N`, commuting with the
shift. Then for all objects `x`, `y` of `K(C)`, every object `e` of the endomorphism
differential graded category of `x`, and every integer `n`,

`H^n((L h_y)(x)) ≃ Hom_{DA}(q x, (q y)⟦n⟧)`.

The left-hand side is the explicit cohomology
`DGCategory.RightModule.gradedCohomology` of the evaluation `ev_x (L h_y)`, which is the complex
step 2 of the proof retains the `C(x, x)`-action on. The three links are composed in the order
Yoneda, reflector, source comparison; the first and third are used in the inverse direction. -/
def chainEquivReflectorEvaluation
    {L : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K} [L.CommShift ℤ]
    {η : 𝟭 (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⟶ L}
    (hL : ∀ X, (yonedaLocalizing C G).rightOrthogonal (L.obj X))
    (hη : ∀ (X Z : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K) (f : Z ⟶ X) (g : L.obj X ⟶ Z⟦(1 : ℤ)⟧),
      Triangle.mk f (η.app X) g ∈ distTriang (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K →
        yonedaLocalizing C G Z)
    {DA : Type u'} [Category.{v'} DA] [HasShift DA ℤ] (q : C.K ⥤ DA)
    [q.IsLocalization (yonedaInverseImage C G).trW] [q.CommShift ℤ]
    (x y : C.K) (e : (endDGCategory C (x : C.Obj)).Obj) (n : ℤ) :
    gradedCohomology ((evaluationDGFunctor.{v} C (x : C.Obj)).obj
        (L.obj (yonedaObjK (y : C.Obj)))) e n ≃ (q.obj x ⟶ (q.obj y)⟦n⟧) :=
  ((homShiftEquivEvaluationGradedCohomology (L.obj (yonedaObjK (y : C.Obj)))
      (x : C.Obj) e n).symm.trans
    (homEquivReflectorShift (ofObj fun i ↦ yonedaObjK (G i))
      (ofObj fun i ↦ yonedaObjK (G i)).localizingClosure.{v}.trW.Q hL hη
      (yonedaObjK (x : C.Obj)) (yonedaObjK (y : C.Obj)) n)).trans
    (homEquivDerivedYonedaOnK' C G q x y n).symm

/-- **The chain `(*)` with the reflector supplied.** Step 1 of [Stacks, Tag 09LK] produces an
exact reflector onto the `N`-local objects whose unit has fibres in `N`
(`DGCategory.RightModule.exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK_of_dgCategory`), so the
composite of `DGCategory.RightModule.chainEquivReflectorEvaluation` exists for any localization
`q` of `K(C)` at `Z = Φ⁻¹ N`: there are an exact `L` and bijections

`H^n((L h_y)(x)) ≃ Hom_{DA}(q x, (q y)⟦n⟧)`

natural in nothing — the statement is object by object, which is all the chain gives. -/
theorem exists_chainEquivReflectorEvaluation {DA : Type u'} [Category.{v'} DA]
    [HasShift DA ℤ] (q : C.K ⥤ DA)
    [q.IsLocalization (yonedaInverseImage C G).trW] [q.CommShift ℤ] :
    ∃ (L : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K)
      (_ : L.CommShift ℤ) (_ : L.IsTriangulated),
      ∀ (x y : C.K) (e : (endDGCategory C (x : C.Obj)).Obj) (n : ℤ),
        Nonempty (gradedCohomology ((evaluationDGFunctor.{v} C (x : C.Obj)).obj
          (L.obj (yonedaObjK (y : C.Obj)))) e n ≃ (q.obj x ⟶ (q.obj y)⟦n⟧)) := by
  obtain ⟨L, cs, tri, η, h₁, -, h₃⟩ :=
    exists_isTriangulated_reflector_yonedaObjK_of_dgCategory C G
  exact ⟨L, cs, tri, fun x y e n ↦
    ⟨chainEquivReflectorEvaluation C G h₁ h₃ q x y e n⟩⟩

/-! ### The one datum the chain does not supply -/

omit [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).CommShift ℤ] [((yonedaDGFunctor C).onK).IsTriangulated] in
/-- **The localization hypothesis of the chain, from an identification of `Z`.** The right-hand
side of `DGCategory.RightModule.chainEquivReflectorEvaluation` is a Hom group of a localization
of `K(C)` at `Z = Φ⁻¹ N`. To read it as a Hom group of the derived category of an abelian
category one needs a localization of `K(C)` at the *acyclic* complexes to be a localization at
`Z`, and that is exactly an equality of the two subcategories.

This records the implication in the only direction that is formal. It is stated so that the gap
is a named hypothesis rather than an implicit mismatch of instances: supplying `hZ` is supplying
the identification of the differential graded localization with the derived category, and
there are two routes to it in this development. `DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_eq`
asks for the existence of `Ac`-resolutions, which is strictly stronger than `A` being abelian;
`DGCategory.RightModule.yonedaInverseImage_eq_of_isTriangulated` asks instead that `Ac` be
triangulated, which costs nothing at `CochainComplex.dgCategoryKAcyclic`, and that the family
enumerate the acyclics up to isomorphism, which is free at the tautological enumeration. The
second route is the one `CochainComplex.derivedHomPhiQh` takes, so no resolution hypothesis
reaches Tag 09LK. -/
theorem isLocalization_trW_of_yonedaInverseImage_eq {DA : Type u'} [Category.{v'} DA]
    (Ac : ObjectProperty C.K) (q : C.K ⥤ DA) [q.IsLocalization Ac.trW]
    (hZ : yonedaInverseImage C G = Ac) :
    q.IsLocalization (yonedaInverseImage C G).trW := by
  rw [hZ]; infer_instance

/-- **The chain `(*)` against a localization at the acyclic complexes.** Let `Ac` be a
subcategory of `K(C)` with `Φ⁻¹ N = Ac` and let `q : K(C) ⥤ DA` be a localization of `K(C)` at
the morphisms whose cone lies in `Ac`, commuting with the shift. Then for every `x`, `y` and `n`

`H^n((L h_y)(x)) ≃ Hom_{DA}(q x, (q y)⟦n⟧)`

for the reflector `L` of step 1. In the intended reading `C` is the differential graded category
of complexes of an abelian category, `Ac` the acyclic complexes and `DA = D(A)`, and the
right-hand side is the group `Hom_{D(A)}(q x, (q y)⟦n⟧)` that the identification `(*)` of step 3
(`CochainComplex.DerivedHomLiftIdentification`) asks the left-hand side to be identified with.

The hypothesis `hZ` is the whole of what is owed: everything else in the chain is
unconditional. -/
theorem exists_chainEquivReflectorEvaluation_of_yonedaInverseImage_eq {DA : Type u'}
    [Category.{v'} DA] [HasShift DA ℤ] (Ac : ObjectProperty C.K) (q : C.K ⥤ DA)
    [q.IsLocalization Ac.trW] [q.CommShift ℤ] (hZ : yonedaInverseImage C G = Ac) :
    ∃ (L : (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K ⥤ (rightModuleCategory.{v} C).K)
      (_ : L.CommShift ℤ) (_ : L.IsTriangulated),
      ∀ (x y : C.K) (e : (endDGCategory C (x : C.Obj)).Obj) (n : ℤ),
        Nonempty (gradedCohomology ((evaluationDGFunctor.{v} C (x : C.Obj)).obj
          (L.obj (yonedaObjK (y : C.Obj)))) e n ≃ (q.obj x ⟶ (q.obj y)⟦n⟧)) :=
  have := isLocalization_trW_of_yonedaInverseImage_eq C G Ac q hZ
  exists_chainEquivReflectorEvaluation C G q

end

end RightModule

end DGCategory

end
